{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implement everything in Go (Fabric's native language) as a standalone Go module for the config-transaction library (U2-U8), plus a fork/branch of the Fabric codebase for the core validation change (U1).",
    "For U2: copy and adapt the genesisconfig profile structures (Profile, Application, Orderer, Consortium, Consortiums, Capabilities, Policies) into the new package with no viper/yaml and no network dependency, but reuse Fabric's common libraries (protolator, policies, msp, common protos) as module dependencies since only genesisconfig usage is prohibited.",
    "Use the functional-options pattern (type Option func(options)) for extensibility as indicated in the U2 API sketch.",
    "For U1: extend the read set (KVRWSet read entries) with an optional SHA-256 hash of the read value rather than the raw value, bounding read-set size while still allowing validators to detect tampered endorser state; entries without a hash fall back to legacy version-only checks for backward compatibility.",
    "For U1: modify the endorser's transaction simulator/rwset builder to record value hashes for point reads, and extend MVCC/state-based validation so a transaction is invalidated when a read entry's hash does not match the committing peer's local state.",
    "Use deterministic proto marshaling and canonical field ordering so generated blocks/updates can be compared with configtxgen/configtxlator output via proto.Equal, as required by the acceptance criteria.",
    "Represent detached signatures as ConfigSignature protos (SignatureHeader + signature computed over the concatenation of signature header bytes and ConfigUpdate bytes), matching Fabric's existing signing semantics so signatures are interchangeable with the peer CLI.",
    "Structure the library around a small set of internal helpers (get/set on ConfigGroup/ConfigValue/ConfigPolicy, MSP config generation, ConfigUpdate computation) that the user-facing functions for U2, U5, U6, U7 and U8 compose, avoiding duplicated logic.",
    "Adopt golden-file equivalence testing: fixtures generated by configtxgen, configtxlator, cryptogen and the peer signtx flow are stored and compared against library output for each acceptance criterion.",
    "For U1 integration verification, run a small Fabric network (2 orgs, multiple peers), tamper one endorsing peer's world state, and assert the transaction is invalidated and not committed by the remaining peers."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "All work is performed by a single developer (the author) who is already experienced with Go and with Hyperledger Fabric internals; no learning/onboarding time is counted beyond the design activities.",
    "Target Fabric version is 2.x LTS (the spec references both 1.4 and 2.0 documentation; 2.x is assumed).",
    "Effort figures are work-hours (not calendar time) and include unit tests within each implementation activity; integration/equivalence testing, rework and documentation are separate activities.",
    "A working development environment, the Fabric source tree and its integration test suite are already available; environment procurement time is limited to the small scaffolding activity.",
    "Reusing Fabric's common packages (protolator, policies, msp, protos) as library dependencies is acceptable; only direct use of genesisconfig/viper/yaml processing is prohibited per U2.",
    "For U1, scope is limited to point (KV) reads; range-query validation semantics are left unchanged.",
    "Key material is always supplied to the library as PEM/DER bytes or Go crypto types; secure key storage and HSM integration are out of scope.",
    "U2 genesis block generation must support the prototypical integration-test configtx.yaml profile, including etcdraft (and solo) consensus settings, application and orderer orgs, capabilities and policies; exotic configtx.yaml features not present in the reference profile are out of scope.",
    "Code review feedback arrives asynchronously (open-source style); expected review/rework effort is captured in a dedicated activity rather than per-story padding.",
    "Documentation scope is GoDoc plus a README with usage examples; no external documentation site is produced.",
    "U8 covers only adding the organization to a consortium in the system channel configuration; channel creation from the updated consortium is explicitly out of scope per the story."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and library API/architecture design",
      "activity_description": "Analyze U2-U8, define the package layout and public function signatures of the config-transaction library, map each acceptance criterion to a concrete implementation approach, and identify reusable internal helpers (config group get/set, MSP generation, update computation).",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Repository, build and CI scaffolding",
      "activity_description": "Create the Go module, directory layout, lint/vet configuration, test runner and continuous-integration pipeline for the new library, plus a working branch of Fabric for U1.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U1 design: tampered read-set detection approach",
      "activity_description": "Investigate the endorser, rwset builder, tx simulator, MVCC and state-based validation paths; design the backward-compatible read-set value-hash extension and specify where the tamper check is enforced at validation/commit time.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U1 implementation: rwset extension and endorser capture",
      "activity_description": "Extend the rwset proto/read structures with an optional value hash, update the transaction simulator and rwset builder to record hashes of read values during chaincode execution, and regenerate/handle proto code. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U1 implementation: validator-side tamper detection",
      "activity_description": "Extend MVCC/state-based validation (including the CouchDB variant) to compare read-entry value hashes against the committing peer's local state and mark mismatched transactions invalid, preserving legacy behavior when hashes are absent. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 36
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U1 tests: integration test with tampered peer",
      "activity_description": "Build an integration test that stands up a multi-peer network, tampers one endorsing peer's world state, executes a chaincode transaction, and asserts the transaction is invalidated and not committed by honest peers (reproducing the referenced article's scenario).",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Copy/adapt genesisconfig profile structures",
      "activity_description": "Port the Profile, Application, Orderer, Consortium, Consortiums, Capabilities and Policies types from genesisconfig into the new package, removing viper/yaml coupling and shaping them as plain input data structures per U2. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Core ConfigGroup/ConfigValue/ConfigPolicy helper utilities",
      "activity_description": "Implement internal helpers to traverse and mutate ConfigGroup trees (get/set values and policies, mod policy handling, version management) with deterministic marshaling, forming the foundation for U2, U5, U7 and U8. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 28
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "MSP configuration generation from raw crypto material",
      "activity_description": "Implement generation of a FabricMSPConfig (root/intermediate/admin certs, revocation lists, OU identifiers, crypto config) directly from supplied PEM material without reading an MSP folder, shared by U2 and U6. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U6: Organization ConfigGroup generation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the public function that builds a semantically complete organization ConfigGroup (MSP value plus Admins/Writers/Readers signature policies, anchor peers where applicable) equivalent to cryptogen + configtxgen -printOrg output. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 28
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U7: ConfigUpdate computation from base and modified configs",
      "activity_description": "Implement recursive comparison of two Config trees to compute the read set, write set and mod policies of a ConfigUpdate, matching configtxlator compute_update semantics, with only the two transactions as input. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U2: Channel creation transaction / genesis block generation",
      "activity_description": "Implement CreateChannelTx(channelSpec, ...Option) that builds the full channel configuration (orderer, application, consortiums, capabilities, policies, consensus parameters) and produces a proto-encoded genesis block that is proto.Equal to configtxgen output for the reference profile. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U3: Detached signature generation for config updates",
      "activity_description": "Implement the function that signs a marshaled ConfigUpdate with caller-supplied key material, producing a ConfigSignature (signature header + signature) usable as one of n required signatures. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "U4: Assembly of signed config update envelope",
      "activity_description": "Implement the function that combines a ConfigUpdate with a set of detached ConfigSignatures into a complete CONFIG_UPDATE Envelope acceptable to orderers and peers, equivalent to signatures accumulated via the peer CLI. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "U5: Batch size (max_message_count) update transaction",
      "activity_description": "Implement the function that takes an existing channel configuration and produces an unsigned ConfigUpdate modifying the orderer batch size max_message_count, composed from the A8/A11 helpers. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "U8: Add organization to consortium in system channel",
      "activity_description": "Implement the function that takes a system-channel configuration and an organization definition and produces an unsigned ConfigUpdate adding the org to the named consortium, equivalent to the manual printOrg/protolator/configtxlator flow. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "Equivalence and integration test suite",
      "activity_description": "Build golden-file fixtures from configtxgen, configtxlator, cryptogen and the peer signtx flow; write cross-story integration tests asserting proto.Equal/semantic equivalence for every acceptance criterion (U2-U8), including end-to-end sign-and-assemble flows.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "Defect fixing, refactoring and review rework",
      "activity_description": "Address defects found by the equivalence/integration tests, refactor duplicated logic across stories, and incorporate code review feedback on both the library and the U1 core change.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and usage examples",
      "activity_description": "Write GoDoc for all public functions and types, plus a README with worked examples for channel creation, config update signing/assembly, batch-size update, org generation, update computation and consortium addition.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "Final verification and release packaging",
      "activity_description": "Run the full test suites (unit, equivalence, Fabric integration for U1), verify acceptance criteria one final time, tag/version the library module and prepare the U1 patch set for submission.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 520
  }
}

